% Generate `lib/app_paths.py`: OpenNolan's single source of truth for WHERE it reads
% code (read-only) vs. WHERE it writes user data (writable). The split exists so the
% notarized Mac app — a read-only `.app` bundle — keeps code in the bundle while user
% data lives outside it (e.g. `~/Library/Application Support/OpenNolan`).
% Use `from __future__ import annotations`; import only `os` and `pathlib.Path`.

Compute `_REPO_ROOT` once at import as the repo checkout root — the parent of `lib/`,
i.e. `Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent`. It is the historical default for every
path, so dev is behavior-preserving: with no env vars set, everything resolves under it.

Every function returns a `Path` and reads `os.environ` on EACH call (never cached at
import), so a subprocess that sets these vars is picked up live.

Two independent roots — do not conflate them:

- `code_root()` — read-only code/skills/tools/guides root. `OPENNOLAN_CODE_ROOT` or `_REPO_ROOT`.
- `home()` — writable data root. `OPENNOLAN_HOME` or `_REPO_ROOT`.

These derive from `home()`, but an explicit per-path override env var wins when set:

| function            | override env var            | default            |
|---------------------|-----------------------------|--------------------|
| `projects_dir()`    | `OPENNOLAN_PROJECTS_DIR`     | `home()/projects`  |
| `env_path()`        | `OPENNOLAN_ENV_FILE`         | `home()/.env`      |
| `user_styles_dir()` | `OPENNOLAN_USER_STYLES_DIR`  | `home()/user_styles` |
| `runtime_dir()`     | `OPENNOLAN_RUNTIME_DIR`      | `home()/runtime`   |
| `cache_dir()`       | `OPENNOLAN_CACHE_DIR`        | `home()/cache`     |

Purpose hints for the docstrings: `projects_dir` = per-project artifacts/assets/renders/
checkpoints; `env_path` = the BYOK `.env`; `user_styles_dir` = user-dropped style playbooks,
kept OUT of the read-only built-in `styles/` dir and merged in by `styles/playbook_loader.py`;
`runtime_dir` = managed venv + downloaded ffmpeg + capability packs; `cache_dir` = ML
framework caches (HF_HOME/TRANSFORMERS_CACHE/piper/rembg).

- `is_packaged() -> bool` — True when running inside the packaged Mac app. Return
  `bool(os.environ.get("OPENNOLAN_CODE_ROOT"))`: the Electron shell sets that var only in a
  packaged build, so it is the single signal gating packaged-only behavior (the restricted
  pipeline/style catalogue and the agent's filesystem sandbox).
